A||||5||BUCK WILLIAMS||86 gt right headlight motor wont cut off!!||||5||
Z||000000||BUCK WILLIAMS||12-13-2001||10:10 AM||||my 86 gt right front headlight motor wont cut off once the light is up.  can anyone tell me how to fix this?  thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroPerformance||12-13-2001||04:57 PM||||You can unhook the wires and let it stay in the up position. I had the same problem and I ended up replacing mine. The problem is that there is a switch in there that is supposed to shut it off when the headlight reaches to up position and the switch has gone bad. I believe that <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  has rebuild kits for headlight motors but I dont know what years they work with.<P>-Charlie<BR> <A HREF="http://www.customcellularproducts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customcellularproducts.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blacktree||12-13-2001||05:03 PM||||Another common cause for that problem is a worn out gear in the headlamp actuator assembly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||85ZainoGT||12-13-2001||06:47 PM||||yup, sounds like a stripped gear, thats what my problem was, buy a gear from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  for your year.. good luck!  You may need to buy screws, I was sent the wrongones with my order from him!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||BUCK WILLIAMS||12-14-2001||05:22 PM||||THANKS FOR YOUR HELP. HAVE A GOOD FIERO WEEKEND!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000005||CountFiero||12-14-2001||05:37 PM||||With mine, ('84 SE 2m4)I just ran a couple of wires off of that motor and mounted a toggle switch under the dash.  Switch off the lights as usual--they go down, then hit the toggle switch and the motor stops "running". They will still go UP/ON as usual. That way you avoid the infamous "WINKING FIERO" and you can maintain the cars natural GOOD LOOKS.  Running with the lights UP, and Not ON looks LAME.<BR>Eventually you MAY want to replace the motor but this method will save you having to do the repair TODAY.  And it's ALOT LESS labor intensive than changing the motor.  I still run my lights using the toggle switch.  ||||reg||1
